data_structure
#
# A REAL fold, off this booth's own hardware: the Dickerson-Drew dodecamer
# (examples/dna_dickerson.yaml -- CGCGAATTCGCG paired with itself) folded by
# protenix-v2 on a Blackhole card, 2026-08-13, warm, 4.57s, mean pLDDT 95.7.
# Copied verbatim out of the runner's own structures directory; nothing here
# is hand-edited, which is the point -- it is exactly the file
# `ui.geometry.ribbon_from_cif` is handed at the booth.
#
# What makes it worth 54 KB in the tree: it is the first NON-PROTEIN
# structure in this suite. Two chains of 12 nucleotides, 494 atoms, residues
# DA/DC/DG/DT, and not one atom named "CA" anywhere in it -- so it is the
# fixture that fails the moment `load_backbone_trace` forgets that a
# nucleic-acid residue anchors on its phosphate. It is also a genuinely
# awkward shape to test against, and deliberately kept for that: the two
# strands are near-identical (the sequence is its own reverse complement),
# which is exactly the symmetry that would hide a chain-assignment bug, so
# the assertions that use it have to be about POSITION -- see
# tests/unit/test_geometry_mesh.py's duplex tests, which forbid geometry in
# the 18.8 A gap between strand A's 3' end and strand B's 5' end rather than
# counting things that both strands have equal numbers of.
#
